{"title":"G285 2021 MC10B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1f0a94ea8742b3593b3b394c54f3ad77a4b1de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lceil {\\frac{3!+4!+5!+6!}{2+3+4+5+6}} \\right \\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"154\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/89135b84ce4ab65534a21b1009c6c69749fa7467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 43\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 44\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 45\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa5237ca39f572352a5eab95e5acb05cd214c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$deg(Q(x))=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/daeba2a1bd1d860d83adededa199ff54b12c4a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$deg(K(x))=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d63e883c87abdc9cb603bdc1d82423baf22bdce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)=(x-2)K(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4379d61402d0206f1444505dcc1138a8a96c44e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$deg(Q(x)-2K(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad07ba45d9a4dcd46fbd971320abb2585f7ce0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A convex hexagon of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is inscribed in a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108b5fe90572221ce15300e946f49a14c093e090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\neq s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/002f464e6f6dd71f28b4f64261c14e2837cee121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{2r}=\\frac{21}{29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41af23d1af501d104f279cbf5148458837354074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=58$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />, find the area of the hexagon.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26ad26f21b7ec053f7f3c6e7392aa566eb97d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 60\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 84\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 90\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0ecf55708a67bff9f999ca0685fcf917c6b68bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{9}\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/4380d9213f8d52b494d76486ebbe5f42b7e15a52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2n \\equiv 7 \\pmod{13}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/102cbaaf18d401b022636fc5a9b0d2f878eaf510.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5n \\equiv 14 \\pmod{17}\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60758040e515473e6dd2f24e880b5cccc6769e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1560\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1713\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2211\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3273\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3702$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"484\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A principal is pushing out an emergency COVID-19 alert to his school of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> teachers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> students. Suppose the announcement is first approved by his <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> aides. Then, each of the aides share the announcement to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> teachers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> students, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e44743bd3c3f38fc8ff8945be5e94885a9f0cdd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,t \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> and for every aide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1af89e7ea6806c8c9ae4f1be2ff087db1368a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. Moreover, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371a87af475b29b5467819b9621d4ff881498f04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+t = (u+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the round number ( for the aides releasing info it is round 1, then round 2....) After every round <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> teachers in the previous round share the announcement to a new group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> teachers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> students, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f27740b63834c3dc2a7c545ae5081eee8c83af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=(u+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"21\" />. How many rounds will it take until the entire school is informed? Assume that after all teachers are informed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> still grows as if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3f9bd7ea38f7336f5a64109d4053d775858f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/08479664832994dea9abbe888015464b0221bbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> planes parallel to the horizontal slice a sphere with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> at not necessarily distinct random locations to create <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> cross sections, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d464921ad89b0c5fe3f1f302dfb61ebe050a150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> partial spheres. What range of values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> will the cumulative area of the cross-sections never be able to exceed the sum of the outer surface areas of the partial spheres?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76a5e7aa89f5d0629bfc19477fb6c96e36cbdb09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ {1,2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ {1,2,3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ {1,2,3,4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ {2,3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ {2,3,4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"503\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the following infinite summation be shown: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eec04204a00c29c25f462bfb0c62d5864c5fd21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left \\lfloor \\cdots \\sum_{k=2}^{11} \\left \\lfloor -k+ \\sum_{j=2}^{10} {\\left \\lfloor {-j+\\sum_{i=2}^\\infty \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{10i^2+11i-2}{i^3}} \\right \\rfloor} \\right \\rfloor} \\right \\rfloor \\right \\rfloor \\cdots\\]\" width=\"422\" height=\"54\" />\nSuppose each individual sum is denoted by a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc09bf78496a1185a99fff1cecde7acf6347a02a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is the inner most sum, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622661e870ee8b198b115bda6a9a17cd3f6c919c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> evaluates sums going outward. For what minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> will the expression be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/724832e155c6cce1f57c688a926d506c1aca208d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db41bb627454c47f9c8bf31fdea1124afe98a003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{it is never bigger than 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"531\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of all real values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> if:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b985c5c9c0964401ec0ec0fc44684d43cd484fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^{\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 3^x -1} = \\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/9811f9bc37d29716794a63f8d8697ddf22c5c732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_2021_MC10B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a 3-digit positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253750ca96b711987b5b141b598387c39607ec1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$palindromic$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" /> if it can be represented as the difference of two distinct palindromes, and the number itself is NOT a palindrome. Find the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253750ca96b711987b5b141b598387c39607ec1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$palindromic$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37214fbfecdee24d74c3fe6888304d43ed4ddb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$numbers$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/167673661cdc5d7103c53fc3c83fc1f3bc0ef2a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 740\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 820\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 900\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 940\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"448\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G285_MC10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"G285 MC10B Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085217\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 310/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11029/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21271:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018085217 and revision id 154388. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}